# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  .gitignore — what NEVER enters git history
#
#  Philosophy: external code is FETCHED by install.sh, never vendored.
#  Machine state and runtime caches never leave this machine.
#  Directory skeletons survive a fresh clone via tracked .gitkeep files
#  (NOT via negation rules — those leaked embedded git repos as
#  broken gitlinks, which is why this file was rewritten).
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── External (cloned) code — ALL of it, unconditionally ────────────
# Oh My Zsh, Spaceship, and plugins are cloned by install.sh. They
# contain their own .git dirs; tracking them creates broken gitlinks.
# Ignore the entire tree. The skeleton is preserved by the tracked
# .gitkeep files explicitly re-included below.
external/*
external/plugins/*

# Re-include ONLY the empty-dir markers so the structure survives a
# fresh clone (install.sh repopulates the rest).
!external/.gitkeep
!external/plugins/
external/plugins/*
!external/plugins/.gitkeep

# ── Machine-specific overrides — never leave this machine ──────────
local/*
!local/.gitkeep

# ── Runtime cache — zcompdump, history, compcache, etc. ────────────
cache/*
!cache/.gitkeep

# ── Completion dumps written beside the profile ────────────────────
# cache/* above covers the dump this config asks for ($ZSH_COMPDUMP,
# set in modules/00-env.zsh). It does NOT cover dumps written here by
# something that never reads that variable:
#
#   • Debian and Ubuntu run a bare `compinit` from /etc/zsh/zshrc, which
#     is sourced BEFORE ~/.zshrc and so writes to ${ZDOTDIR:-$HOME}
#   • running the test suite sets ZDOTDIR to this directory, which makes
#     ${ZDOTDIR:-$HOME} resolve to exactly here
#
# One of these was committed by a `git add -A` because nothing ignored
# it. A generated 51 KB completion dump has no business in git history.
.zcompdump*

# ── Editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
